& [KnownInput] is the CPMS-I02B result
  + two direction-isolated universes contain five root drafts, closed local definition graphs, exact accounts, fingerprints, profile limits, generator identity, and caller-supplied source revision
  + root resource measurement already constructs an internal root plus transitive closure, but no canonical document or artifact is released
  + base_response and preparation_response have equal raw root bytes today while retaining different root kinds, schema ids, and root fingerprints

& [DocumentQuestion] is how to publish one exact self-contained document per root
  + each document should use Draft 2020-12, its existing stable schema id, the root structure, and exactly its transitive same-direction $defs closure
  + every local reference must resolve within that document
  + document canonical bytes and digest must include $schema, $id, and $defs
  + document metadata must bind direction, root kind, semantic type name, generator, supplied source revision, root fingerprint, universe fingerprint, byte length, and digest without adding provider-private schema keywords

& [BundleQuestion] is how to make the five documents one deterministic compatibility baseline
  + the bundle should carry exact documents and accounts in lexical root-kind order
  + one bundle digest must avoid self-reference by hashing a canonical unsigned payload under a domain-separated profile
  + checked-in golden files should be byte-equal projections of the bundle documents and manifest, not independent authorities
  + source revision identifies the code input used to generate artifacts and need not equal the later commit that contains the generated artifacts

& [CompatibilityQuestion] is bounded
  + I02C may emit an exact baseline signature and detect byte-identical replay
  + any changed same-direction document remains unclassified and release-blocking until a later compatibility algorithm proves direction-appropriate implications
  + a baseline signature is content identity, not a cryptographic signer attestation and not semantic compatibility authority

& [FailureQuestion] is fail closed
  + reject missing or extra roots, direction mismatch, schema-id mismatch, non-object roots, conflicting $schema or preexisting $id or $defs, absent closure members, cross-direction references, resource exhaustion, digest mismatch, golden drift, or partial bundle formation

& [SliceQuestion] is separately signable
  + form exact data, materialization, canonicalization reuse, artifact, baseline, bounds, and proof contracts for CPMS-I02C
  - never: parse untrusted JSON, reject duplicate keys from bytes, validate instances, prove serde equivalence, classify changed schemas as compatible, define provider tools, call a model, persist at runtime, network, effect, production, or hardware
